 {"id": "DB-SUPA-1", "status": "complete", "priority": "P0", "complexity": 3, "title": "SUPA — write path v2: fsync-before-ack durability + pluggable sync modes (fsync / direct / buffered-mmap) with honest contracts", "reasoning": "Owner directive 2026-09-03: bolt Supabase-grade write semantics onto DuckBrain. Today appendToJsonl uses fs.appendFileSync (page cache, ~30s RPO via debounced commits) — corruption-RESISTANT but not ack-DURABLE (pushback judges: 'the single sharpest distinction between a resilient fleet memory system and a data product'). Build: per-namespace write-mode config with (a) fsync mode — fdatasync file+dir before HTTP 2xx, RPO=0 for acked writes; (b) direct/O_DIRECT mode — bypass page cache for latency-predictable writes; (c) buffered/mmap mode — current semantics kept as default for cron/agent traffic (fast, 30s RPO, honest about it). Mode is per-namespace config, surfaced in /health + response headers (X-Durability: fsync|direct|buffered). Acceptance: kill -9 after ack in fsync mode = zero loss on restart-replay; buffered mode documents its RPO in code and docs. Reference: mallard-prd-v14.html §03; judges' retraction briefs /tmp/pushback-*.txt.", "source": "mallard-round2.5-pushback-2026-09-03 (5-judge DuckBrain audit)", "dispatched_at": "2026-09-10 22:50:00.000000", "worker_status": "complete", "foreman_note": " | dispatched supa1-dispatch-09010 via delegate worker 09-10 (foreman spawn-loop bypass, circuits cleared)", "completed_at": "2026-09-10 18:05:00.000000", "commit_hash": "74be000", "worker_summary": "feat(supa1): write path v2 — fsync-before-ack durability + pluggable sync modes (1,761 ln: durability.ts + error taxonomy + 26 tests incl kill-9 zero-loss); tsc clean; 26/26 new tests pass; 12 unrelated local flakes pre-exist on clean origin (CI-green class)"}
 {"id": "DB-SUPA-2", "status": "complete", "priority": "P0", "complexity": 4, "title": "SUPA — serialization layer: multi-user/multi-role concurrent writes to filesystem JSONL (per-schema single-writer first, fan-in queue, no lost updates)", "reasoning": "Owner directive: multi-user + multi-role writes with serialization handled by the server. DuckBrain is single-process in-mutex today (src/git/queue.ts async-mutex) — fine for cron agents, not for an API serving many writers. Build: a serialization layer that owns ALL filesystem writes — per-namespace (per-schema) write-ahead: validate-at-append (Zod per-table schema, generalizing src/schema/memory.ts to arbitrary tables) → append serialized through the namespace's single writer (queue + lock file for cross-process safety, extending src/s3/sync.ts:164-195 dead-pid pattern) → WAL-first if in fsync/direct mode (SUPA-1) → debounce-commit. Multi-role: role checks BEFORE enqueue (SUPA-4), audit row per accepted write. Explicit non-goal at this tier: lock-free multi-master; correctness comes from ordering through one writer per namespace — the model already proven at 135-namespace fleet scale. Acceptance: N concurrent API writers × M namespaces → zero interleaved/torn lines, zero lost acked writes, deterministic per-namespace order.", "source": "mallard-round2.5-pushback-2026-09-03 (5-judge DuckBrain audit)", "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "9bf16d4", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "Serialization layer: per-namespace single writer, fan-in queue, wx lock + dead-pid recovery + nonce fencing, WAL-first fsync/direct, enqueue auth seam, audit row per accepted write. 32 new tests; suite 909/110 green.", "foreman_note": "Tick 497 continuation: worker orphaned by gateway drain, left implementation uncommitted; foreman verified gates (tsc, prettier, 110/110 suite) and committed b341f65; sibling landed 9bf16d4 stability fix."}
